From f07e1bdd6a2c74fcffa8dbc4f8a4555198f37c8e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shanire <shanire86@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 05:31:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Bump lru dependency from 0.16.3 to 0.18.2

RUSTSEC-2026-0253 reports a potential use-after-free in LruCache::pop()
caused by a lack of panic safety; all versions before 0.18.2 are affected.
This moves every crate in the workspace onto the first fixed release.

lru 0.17 and later declare rust-version = 1.85.0, which matches this
repository's MSRV floor, so no MSRV change is required. No source
changes are needed: cargo check --workspace passes unmodified.

Signed-off-by: Shanire <shanire86@gmail.com>
---
 Cargo.toml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Cargo.toml b/Cargo.toml
index d62629c..64d4707 100644
--- a/Cargo.toml
+++ b/Cargo.toml
@@ -43,7 +43,7 @@ log = "0.4"
 futures = "0.3"
 h2 = ">=0.4.14"
 once_cell = "1"
-lru = "0.16.3"
+lru = "0.18.2"
 ahash = ">=0.8.9"
 
 [workspace.lints.rust]
-- 
2.39.5

